From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BunkerWeb Windows port <bunkerweb-windows@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:59:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Templator: render in one worker thread instead of forked
 processes

Templator.render() renders the servers in a ProcessPoolExecutor with the "fork" multiprocessing context (so children
inherit globals). Windows only has "spawn", which would have to pickle the Templator and re-import the generator in
every child (and ValueError: cannot find context for 'fork' otherwise). The rendering is a few Jinja templates per
server, so it is done in a single worker thread.

Upstream: none, Windows specific (no fork); a spawn-safe Templator would remove the need
Check: Templator.render() no longer uses a ProcessPoolExecutor / mp.get_context("fork")

diff --git a/common/gen/Templator.py b/common/gen/Templator.py
index 8f8340b..46d3835 100644
--- a/common/gen/Templator.py
+++ b/common/gen/Templator.py
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 #!/usr/bin/env python3
 
-from concurrent.futures import ProcessPoolExecutor, as_completed
+from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor, as_completed
 from contextlib import suppress
 from ctypes import CDLL, c_char_p, c_int, c_long, c_void_p
 from ctypes.util import find_library
@@ -470,7 +470,7 @@ class Templator:
 
         failures = self._render_global()
         server_start = perf_counter()
-        with ProcessPoolExecutor(max_workers=max_workers, mp_context=mp.get_context("fork")) as executor:
+        with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1) as executor:
             future_to_batch = {}
             for i in range(0, len(servers), batch_size):
                 batch = servers[i : i + batch_size]  # noqa: E203
